      "provider": {
        "name": "deepseek-tri",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "mode": "json_single"
      },
      "summaries": {
        "en": "DETR-ResNet-50 is an end-to-end object detection model that eliminates the need for complex anchor boxes and post-processing steps like non-maximum suppression. Its key innovation is using a transformer encoder-decoder architecture to treat object detection as a set prediction problem, directly outputting bounding boxes and class labels. Researchers can fine-tune it on custom datasets using PyTorch, experiment with different backbone networks, or deploy it via Hugging Face's inference API for real-time detection tasks in applications like autonomous driving or content moderation.",
        "zh": "DETR-ResNet-50是一种端到端的目标检测模型，它摒弃了传统方法中复杂的锚框设计和非极大值抑制等后处理步骤。其核心创新在于采用Transformer编码器-解码器架构，将目标检测转化为集合预测问题，直接输出边界框和类别标签。这种设计简化了检测流程，同时保持了高精度。开发者可通过PyTorch在自定义数据集上微调模型，尝试不同的骨干网络架构，或利用Hugging Face推理API快速部署，适用于自动驾驶、内容审核等需要实时目标识别的场景。",
        "es": "DETR-ResNet-50 is an end-to-end object detection model that eliminates the need for complex anchor boxes and post-processing steps like non-maximum suppression. Its key innovation is using a transformer encoder-decoder architecture to treat object detection as a set prediction problem, directly outputting bounding boxes and class labels. Researchers can fine-tune it on custom datasets using PyTorch, experiment with different backbone networks, or deploy it via Hugging Face's inference API for real-time detection tasks in applications like autonomous driving or content moderation.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "detr-resnet-50 stands out for transformers, pytorch, and safetensors in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "DETR-ResNet-50 is an end-to-end object detection model that eliminates the need for complex anchor boxes and post-processing steps like non-maximum suppression. Its key innovation is using a transformer encoder-decoder architecture to treat object detection as a set prediction problem, directly outputting bounding boxes and class labels. Researchers can fine-tune it on custom datasets using PyTorch, experiment with different backbone networks, or deploy it via Hugging Face's inference API for real-time detection tasks in applications like autonomous driving or content moderation.",
          "how": "Review https://huggingface.co/facebook/detr-resnet-50 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
